--shape LIST                tiny,many-small,few-large,wide-root
--payload LIST              compressible,incompressible
--writer-shape LIST         tiny,large,payload-heavy
--xlsx-shape LIST           tiny,medium,dense-wide
--xlsb-shape LIST           tiny,medium,large,sparse (only used by opt-in XLSB semantic cases)
--xlsx-cell-crud-shape LIST medium,dense-sparse,noncompact,vendor-extension (used by matched scalar-cell and edit-composition cases)
--xlsx-row-visibility-shape LIST medium,large (only used by matched row-visibility cases)
--semantic-shape LIST       tiny,medium,large (only used by opt-in Office semantic cases)
--rtf-variant LIST          plain,byte1252,lzfu,watermark (default: plain)
--range-fixed-latency-us N  Fixed latency per request (default: 100)
--range-request-overhead-us N
Request overhead (default: 25)
--range-bandwidth-bytes-per-sec N
Bandwidth (default: 52428800)
--range-max-physical-bytes N
Maximum physical range (default: 4096)
--workers LIST              Scaling workers: 1,2,4,8,available (capped/deduped)
--opc-cache-lock-diagnostics
Opt in to direct OPC cache/flight mutex acquisition samples
--json PATH                 Write JSON to PATH; use - or omit for stdout
--corpus-manifest PATH      Write schema-2 corpus catalog sidecar and
include its additive reference in the report
--real-file PATH            Office file for the opt-in xlsx_real_file_* selectors
--producer-evidence PATH    Write the producer-shape marker/refusal census
--marker-evidence PATH      Write the marker-shape per-member census of the
*_marker_* and *_marker_control_* corpora
--ole2-file PATH            OLE2 file for the opt-in *_range_source_*,
*_owned_source_control_* and *_facade_file_*
selectors; repeatable, at most one DOC, one XLS
and one PPT per run
--ooxml-file PATH           OOXML file for the opt-in
*_real_file_ordinary_save_* selectors; repeatable,
at most one DOCX, one XLSX and one PPTX per run
--save-durability LEVEL     full, file-only or no-sync: time the ordinary-save
*_lifecycle and *_atomic_publish saves through
save_with_durability at LEVEL (default: save)
